{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"Systems"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"schedule","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"]},{"level":3,"text":"Declare a System","anchor":"Declare-a-System","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the "},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro and give it a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"type":"text","text":" writes components, a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them, and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it by its velocity:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"text":" for you: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also conform a type to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand and write its "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" method, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives the whole world. See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for when to do that."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" require one system to run after or before another; "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and "},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" finds those pairs so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test can keep a schedule free of them."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"anchor":"System-Parameters","title":"System Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","title":"Building and Running Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","title":"Main-Actor Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"anchor":"Built-In-Systems","title":"Built-In Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"title":"UpdateEvents","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UpdateEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UpdateEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has had its chance to read them."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","title":"ambiguities()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"title":"Schedule","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"title":"ForwardChanges","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"title":"SystemProfile","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","kind":"symbol","title":"ResourceWriter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"title":"Ambiguity","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","title":"RemovedComponents